Phonon refiner-only CUDA module for llama.cpp b12132 (applies after ../merged/b12132.patch; git apply ignores
this text). Build with -DGGML_CUDA_PHONON_LEAN=ON (scripts/build-cuda-backend.sh does).

What it removes: device code for every weight type except Q4_K and Q5_K (the refiner's 147 + 7 matmul
tensors), every attention head size except 128, every KV type except F16, the float matmul kernels (mmf, mmvf;
the refiner has no float matmul weights), and cuBLAS (stubs that report NOT_SUPPORTED, so ggml aborts loudly
if one is ever reached). cudart is linked statically: the module's only NVIDIA dependency is libcuda.so.1.

Measured 2026-11-09 on the local RTX 3090 box (CUDA 13.3, sm_86 only, stripped):
  libggml-cuda.so  stock 64.9 MB (+ cuBLAS/cuBLASLt/cudart 572.7 MB)  ->  lean 19.3 MB, no other CUDA library
  gzip             stock 42.3 MB (+ 410.2 MB)                          ->  lean 9.7 MB
  lean, machine code only (CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86-real, no PTX): 14.5 MB, gzip 5.4 MB
Per extra architecture (lean, gzip of the extracted code): SASS 5.9-6.1 MB (sm_75/86/89), 7.0 MB (sm_120a);
PTX 9.2-9.6 MB each, which is why per-arch builds ship SASS only.
Gate: the four LOG.md prompts x llama-simple / llama-completion fa auto / -fa on, md5-identical to stock b12132
(12/12), plus 644- and 1610-token prompts with llama-completion, identical.

